-- title:
--   Hecke operators preserve the kernel of reduction at P
-- statement:
--   Let $M \ge 1$ be a natural number and $p$ a prime not dividing $M$, and let $P$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that the image of $p$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ belongs to the nonunits of $P$; write $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}(P)$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \ne p$ (no condition relating $\ell$ to $M$ is imposed). Consider [`ModularCurve.reductionQExpModL P (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma1 M)`](def/ModularCurve_QExpReductionModL.html#L312), the additive map from $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $q$-expansion function field $\mathbb Q$-generated by the integral form ratios for $\Gamma_1(M)$ to $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ over $k$ of the corresponding $q$-expansion function field over $k$; by definition it is [`ModularCurve.laurentReduction`](def/ModularCurve_QExpReductionModL.html#L146) for the residue map of $P$, that is, the $\mathrm{Pic}^0$-level reduction map attached to the predicate `LaurentReductionInputs` for this data when that predicate holds, and the zero map otherwise. Let $z$ be an element of [`ModularCurve.JOne M`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L186), the group $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(M)$, and suppose its reduction is $0$. Then the reduction of [`ModularCurve.heckeOperatorOneBar M ℓ z`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeModule.html#L36) is also $0$, where `heckeOperatorOneBar M ℓ` is the $\mathbb Z$-linear endomorphism underlying [`ModularCurve.heckeOperatorOneAlong (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) M ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_X1HeckeOperator.html#L192), given by `heckePic0OneBar` applied to the data furnished by `HeckeInputsOneAlong` when that predicate holds and by the zero map otherwise.
--
--   This is the statement that the kernel of Deuring's reduction map on $J_1(M)(\overline{\mathbb Q})$ at a place above a prime $p \nmid M$ is stable under the Hecke correspondence $T_\ell$ for every prime $\ell \ne p$ (the operator usually written $U_\ell$ when $\ell \mid M$), the degree-wise consequence of the compatibility of reduction with the two degeneracy maps through $\Gamma_1(M) \cap \Gamma_0(M\ell)$. It is used to upgrade the statement to stability under the whole Hecke algebra action, in [`ModularCurve.reductionQExpModL_gamma1_heckeAlgOne_smul_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.reductionQExpModL_gamma1_heckeAlgOne_smul_eq_zero).
